  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIfYmOg",
      "title": "compliance: add Compliance Module specs",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 971,
      "body": "## Context\r\n\r\nAn OP Stack chain has no way to condition value crossing its canonical bridge where it cannot be\r\nbypassed. Screening at the sequencer misses deposits submitted to L1, which carry forced inclusion,\r\nand it misses withdrawals, which finalize on L1. \r\n\r\nThese specs describe an optional hook that performs screening. The `OptimismPortal` gains one optional hook\r\naddress. While it is `address(0)`, OP stack default behavior remains unchanged. When set, the Portal offers every\r\nitem to the hook before value reaches its recipient. The hook answers proceed, hold or reject, and a held item\r\nexecutes later on the terms the Portal committed to.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\nNew pages:\r\n\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/overview.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/optimism-portal.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/l1-standard-bridge.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/policy.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/contracts/L1/compliance-module.md`\r\n\r\nChains that set no hook are unaffected.\r\n\r\nCloses [#732](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/732)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T21:25:08Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1448,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIT42BA",
      "title": "deposits: Split fork amendments into per-fork pages",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 969,
      "body": "Makes `deposits.md` describe the Bedrock behaviour only, and moves each fork's deposit changes into a per-fork `deposits.md` page.\n\n- `deposits.md` now states the Bedrock state with no fork-gating. Each rule a later fork changes carries a \"Changed by <fork>\" note linking to that fork's page.\n- Each fork that changes deposit rules has a `deposits.md`: Regolith, Canyon, Ecotone, Isthmus, Jovian, Karst, and Lagoon.\n- The Regolith and Canyon overview pages now link to their `deposits.md`.\n\nThe fork-amendments index should be completed once this lands, so the whole spec is self-consistent and canonical.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T03:52:07Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 821,
      "deletions": 663
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABITcGEQ",
      "title": "deposits: Add fork amendment index",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 965,
      "body": "Adds a table at the top of `deposits.md` that lists each deposit rule and the fork that amended it.\n\nDeposit rules are currently spread across `deposits.md` and seven fork pages. A reviewer must assemble today's rules from all of them, and nothing lists them together. This table gives a single place to check that no fork amendment is missed.\n\nEach row links to the fork's overview page, so the table is a pointer index rather than copied content.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T02:46:06Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 22,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIUD2Ww",
      "title": "deposits: Add invariants",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 970,
      "body": "Adds an \"Invariants\" section to `deposits.md` stating the invariants the deposit rules follow:\n\n1. A deposit transaction must always be valid to include in a block.\n2. Deposits buy their gas on L1.\n3. A deposit always mints on L2 exactly the amount of ETH deposited on L1.\n4. The `sourceHash` of a deposit must be unique, so it must include all identifying components of the deposit.\n\nPlus the cross-component invariant that the gas a deposit consumes is accounted for identically across the execution output and the block gas pool.\n\nThese are the positive invariants the current spec only states as a scattered set of \"No X\" negatives. Invariant 3 combines the two ETH-conservation directions: no ETH is created beyond the deposit, and no deposited ETH is lost.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T04:16:40Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 11,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABITvJFg",
      "title": "deposits: Standardize fork-gating phrasing",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 968,
      "body": "Standardizes how fork-gated rules are phrased, using \"Before <fork>\" and \"Since <fork>\" consistently.\n\nThe page previously mixed five phrasings for the same idea: \"prior to the Regolith upgrade\", \"starting with Regolith\", \"starting from the Regolith upgrade\", \"with Regolith\", and \"before the Regolith upgrade\". A single convention lets a reviewer resolve fork applicability mechanically instead of parsing each phrasing.\n\nThis keeps the existing model where each hard fork is defined as a diff in its own page. It only normalizes the notes on the specific items in `deposits.md` that a later fork changes. It does not pull fork rules onto this page.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T03:29:50Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 10
    }
  ],
